// ── PWA icons (PLAN.md §11.7) ───────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Three PNGs, base64-embedded as source constants. They are NOT files on
// disk: this Worker deploys as one self-contained script with no build
// configuration (see worker.js's file header), so a binary asset either
// lives inline or needs a bundler feature this repo has deliberately never
// adopted. ~100KB of base64 total, against a stylesheet already an order of
// magnitude bigger — the tradeoff is not close.
//
// All three are the SAME mark as FAVICON_SVG (src/chrome.js), the "n."
// monogram, rendered on its 512-unit grid, so the tab icon, the Home Screen
// icon and the notification icon are visibly one mark:
//
//   ground  radial glow #3a42a8 -> #151a3a -> #0b0d14 (centred at 50% 8%)
//   n       one stroked path, white, 62 wide, round caps and joins
//           (M150 380 V258 a86 86 0 0 1 172 0 V380)
//   dot     periwinkle #9db0ff, r34 at 392,364
//   centring  the n + dot group is shifted by (-16,-20) so its visual box
//           sits on the canvas centre; the dot hangs off the n's lower
//           right and would otherwise pull the whole mark off-centre.
//
// What differs between them is framing, and each difference is a platform
// requirement, not a style choice:
//
//   ICON_512          rounded corners (rx 112, 22%), transparent outside
//                     them. The `purpose: "any"` icon — shown as-authored,
//                     so it carries its own corner radius.
//   ICON_MASKABLE_512 full-bleed ground, mark scaled to 80% about the
//                     centre. The `purpose: "maskable"` icon: Android crops
//                     it to a platform mask whose safe zone is a circle of
//                     radius 40% (205px) around the centre; the farthest
//                     mark pixel lands ~150px out, inside it with margin.
//   APPLE_TOUCH_ICON  180x180, full-bleed, NO corner radius — iOS applies
//                     its own mask and squircle, and rounding it here would
//                     round it twice. Mark at full size.
//
// The 512px icons are palette-quantized to 256 colours with NO dithering:
// the gradient ground makes the raw renders ~100KB each, and the palette
// cuts that ~2.4x. Dithering was tried and rejected — it leaves visible
// specks in the glow highlight. The 180px apple icon is stored as the raw
// full-colour render (~14KB), since it is small anyway. Regenerating: render
// the SVG geometry above in headless Chromium at the exact pixel size
// (deviceScaleFactor 1, omitBackground for the transparent-corner one), then
// quantize the two 512px renders (sharp: palette, 256 colours, dither 0),
// then bump ICON_VERSION (see CACHE-BUSTING below).
// Deliberately no generator script in this subtree — it is a Node/prettier
// subtree (see the repo CLAUDE.md), and a one-off rasterizer does not get to
// live here.
//
// CACHE-BUSTING: iOS/Safari cache an icon by its URL, so a changed icon
// served at an unchanged URL keeps showing the OLD one on a Home Screen.
// Every reference (chrome.js <link>s, the manifest, the notification icon)
// therefore uses the versioned path built here, and worker.js serves the
// same bytes at both the versioned (immutable) and the legacy unversioned
// (86400s) path. WHEN ANY ICON'S BYTES CHANGE (favicon geometry included),
// BUMP ICON_VERSION below, otherwise iOS keeps showing the old icon.

export const ICON_VERSION = "v2";

/** "/icon-512.png" + "v2" -> "/icon-512.v2.png". */
export function versionedIconPath(path, version = ICON_VERSION) {
  return path.replace(/\.([a-z]+)$/, `.${version}.$1`);
}

export const FAVICON_HREF = versionedIconPath("/favicon.svg");
export const ICON_512_HREF = versionedIconPath("/icon-512.png");
export const ICON_MASKABLE_512_HREF = versionedIconPath("/icon-maskable-512.png");
export const APPLE_TOUCH_ICON_HREF = versionedIconPath("/apple-touch-icon.png");

